<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Wherein&nbsp;I&nbsp;try&nbsp;to&nbsp;make&nbsp;up&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;fact&nbsp;my&nbsp;in-article&nbsp;explanation&nbsp;wasn't&nbsp;very&nbsp;clear.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">3deep5u</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Sorry, but there's not much of a link between this and the other things that I have written (although that may change soon); the connections between this and 1474/2214 mostly have to do with the fact that I have a fever that can only be cured by writing about socialism and mysterious, incomprehensible forces. Also thanks!</p>
<p>The SCP-2387 phenomenon is essentially the physical manifestation from the psychic flotsam of rapid changes in Chinese society.</p>
<p>Billions, if not trillions, of conversations, debates, revolutionary slogans, advertising slogans, and half-remembered thoughts, all regarding how the world is changing and <em>how it should be changed</em> collide in an infinity of different ways over seconds, hours, days, and years. Eventually, the sheer weight of all of this <em>stuff</em> coalesces into an entity. In the sixties, it was revolutionary fervor. In the eighties onward, it became neoliberalism. Hence the bastardized (and apocryphal) Deng quote about how &quot;to get rich is glorious&quot; and the talk about how &quot;this was all stalls&quot; (presumably the &quot;this&quot; in whatever conversation was being cannibalized is now luxury apartments)</p>
<p>The entity responsible for SCP-2387 is not something capable of any sort of thought or even choice as we would recognize it; it operates on blind instinct more than anything. And that instinct says that the new paradigm must be manifested in terms of buildings. In the sixties, this meant replacing peasant huts with the communal farms made from the Unreinforced Concrete of the People, while today, it means whatever the most obscenely expensive kinds of buildings on the market today.</p>
<p>So yeah, SCP-2387 is not some extra-dimensional entity, or some god trying and failing to understand humanity. It is people and the way that they think.</p>
<p>Unless you have a cooler idea, in which case lol jk, your idea is actually the one that I meant.</p>
</div>
